# Video Editor Mobile — Phase Three Final Plan

The Awtsmoos lets a short screen remain a complete vessel rather than a diminished one;
Awtsmoos.com will save space through hierarchy and retraction, never by shrinking the action beneath the thumb.

## Files to touch

1. `apps/video-editor/css/adaptive-motion.css`
   - keep the short-height grid and safe-area transport padding;
   - change short-height transport minimum from 40px to 44px;
   - preserve reduced-motion rules.

2. `apps/video-editor/css/controls.css`
   - preserve the existing 44px control floor, palette, spacing, backdrop, and universal `:active` press;
   - give the three interactive control families one short transition for border/background/transform;
   - move hover styling into `(hover:hover) and (pointer:fine)` so touch does not inherit sticky hover presentation;
   - preserve the active state on every pointer type.

3. `apps/video-editor/index.html`, only after targeted CompactJS compile passes for `js/app.js`.
   - preserve all markup exactly;
   - change only module entry to `./js/app.js?compact=true`.

## Verification

- targeted CompactJS compile + Node syntax check before changing the HTML entry;
- source <=120 lines, tabs, no >160-character lines, diff check clean;
- rerun 320×568 and 390×560 real controller probe;
- require transport buttons >=44px;
- require overflowX/Y 0;
- require drawer fully contained open and fully off-canvas closed;
- require Timeline retract=54px and minimize=150px with no raw tail;
- require no runtime exceptions.

## Completion threshold

If those exact measurements pass, do not redesign the editor further. The drawer, preview/timeline split, horizontal timeline scroll, and retract/minimize architecture are already evidence-proven and should remain simple rather than accumulating unnecessary visual machinery.
